<title>PHILIPPINES: Empire hurt by property woes, hits year-low.</title>
<headline>Empire hurt by property woes, hits year-low.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Empire East Land Holdings Inc dipped to its year low, shedding 60 centavos, or 10.34 percent, to 5.20 pesos in late trade on Friday on fears of an oversupply in the property sector, brokers said.</p>
<p>&quot;There's still the overhang on the property sector... there's a glut especially on the high end and loan problems for the low end,&quot; said Michael Julian, dealer at Philippine Asia Equity Securities.</p>
